  "reason": "The current best (config_021, acc=0.725) uses scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted. The RNA encoder has been the most impactful variable in this search (PCA→scvi gave +0.039), yet scgpt remains completely untested. config_048 isolates this single change (scgpt replacing scvi_n200) while keeping all other settings at their best-known values (imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted, multiprofile). This directly tests whether a more expressive generative RNA encoder can push accuracy beyond 0.725. With 5 experiments remaining, resolving the RNA-encoder question is the highest-value uncertainty to reduce: if scgpt helps, it sets the foundation for further refinement; if it doesn't, we can confidently lock in scvi_n200 and focus remaining budget on fusion or other micro-tuning. Expected relative cost: moderate (~5–7 GPU hours), since scgpt is a larger generative model than scvi_n200 but the overall pipeline (ViT-L + transformer aggregation) was only 3.60 GPU hours with scvi, so the total should remain well under 8 GPU hours."
